On Wed, 22 Nov 2006, azgor wrote:
>
> [1]: Snakes have an engulfing attack, which works only against monsters
> smaller than them. "The python swallows the woodchuck!" --Grunt

   Interesting, easy to patch; but not realistic, IMO. Snakes take a
relatively long time to swallow anything; it's not something they'd
want to do in combat.
   Maybe snakes would "swallow" corpses instead of "eating noisily",
though, and therefore spend less time immobilized by eating. (Yeah,
IRL snakes spend a lot /more/ time immobile than dogs, but hey,
consistency is for hobgoblins.)  This idea could be incorporated into
a comprehensive "eating" patch that would fix other YANIs: "The elf
is eating daintily.", for example.

> [2]: Wishing for "anything", "something", "surprise me", or "nothing",
> should give you either a random item or nothing as appropriate. Wishing
> for stereotypical wishes like "peace on earth" should give a funny
> message, like "Yeah, me too." --azgor

   Problem is, what kind of random item should you get?  I'd say it
ought to be something interesting, most of the time --- something that
the player wouldn't think to wish for on his own. An icebox full of
woodchuck corpses, or one of the lesser-used artifacts. And a small
chance of another wish-granting item, just to give experts an incentive
to say "surprise me".
   Too much AI for me. I did play around with the "malicious genie"
YANI a while back, but never got farther than cursing/rotting/obvious
stuff. Nowhere close to "Sent in some gray dragons."

> [3]: Conduct: tame at least one of every tameable monster. Call it the
> 'Pokemon' conduct: "Gotta catch 'em all!" --Veinor

   That's not how Nethack conducts work; they're things you /don't/ do.
But that's a good thing to add to the Stupid Ascension Tricks list, no? :)


> [10]: Killing a troll with fire or acid or trollsbane should stop it
> from regenerating. --greqrg

   I thought Trollsbane actually /did/ stop it. If not, that's a good YANI.
The fire part is overpowered, though; think "fireball". And AFAICT,
if you're to the level where you can kill a troll with a potion of acid,
or poly into an <acid-colored> dragon just for troll hunting, you really
don't need any help from the game.

   Can you #dip a troll corpse into a potion of acid? I'd be neutral on
that method's stopping the regeneration.

> [12]: New conduct: Fearlessness (You never engraved Elbereth.)
> --TheShrewdDude

   This would /not/ be hard to implement, contrary to some reports. The
game knows exactly when "Elbereth" is engraved, because it keeps monsters
away. I think it's a random engraving too, though, so you'd have to
decide whether teleporting a random Elbereth around the dungeon counts
as using Elbereth. ;) ;)

